### Interview Experience :

Interview started with my Introduction. Then they firstly deep dived my Resume Projects, firstly towards my ML Project which was a Regression Model. They told me to describe about this project, which model I have used, how data preprocessing is done, results, from where I collected the dataset etc. questions based on project and what mentioned in my resume. I tried my best to answer every questions asked. They have my resume infront of them. Then they asked about my second project i.e A Full Stack Web Application Project. They asked me questions such as why I used MongoDB as database and why not MySQL etc.

Then they shifted towards the programming language, they told they are looking for C/C++ or Python language candidates. Java is not used in Intel i guess. I told that I am much comfortable in C++ language, so they asked questions related to Pointers, Array with Pointers, how to reverse a string without using any inbuilt function, OOPS concepts such as Polymorphism and its types with code implementation, about virtual functions, race condition etc.

They also asked that when did I completed my mentioned projects i.e the timeline of my resume projects.

I am attaching the exact code snippets which were given to me,

#include <iostream>

using namespace std;

class Base {

public:

virtual void show() {

cout << "Base";

}

};

class Derived : public Base {

public:

void show() {

cout << "Derived";

}

};

int main() {

Base\* b = new Derived();

b->show();

}

Output :

Derived

